    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the undisputed anchor of the lineup. With a score of 81.24, his matchup against Elder presents the ideal confluence of elite sprint speed\u2014our highest priority\u2014and a favorable 4.40 xERA matchup. **Mickey Moniak** (66.51) also grades out as a primary play; his score is significantly bolstered by a 14% platoon advantage and a wind-out projection, turning his base profile into a high-upside start. Similarly, **Max Muncy** (71.26) is a high-value play despite the lower lineup spot, as the 5.29 xERA of Bradford allows him to exploit a massive 19% SP skill advantage. We are also leaning on **Josh Naylor** (64.61) and **Seiya Suzuki** (61.71) to provide the necessary floor, with **Seiya Suzuki** particularly benefiting from an advantageous #2 hole in the order.\n\nOur most difficult decision came at the bottom of the roster, where **Jose Caballero** (41.62) and **Zach McKinstry** (41.11) both lingered near the threshold. **Jose Caballero** ultimately holds the edge, largely because his elite speed profile is too critical to sacrifice, even against a tough arm like Cease. While we are currently carrying **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** on the deeper bench, none provided the daily efficiency to displace our starters today. We remain cautious regarding the status of **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, whose continued presence on the IL limits our roster flexibility. While **Brice Turang** was considered, his absence from the starting lineup today effectively removed him from consideration for this rotation. Managers should monitor **Gabriel Moreno** closely; despite a solid 64.15 score, he is facing Elder, and any further tightening of the weather or mid-game substitutions could impact his ability to reach his full scoring potential.",
